    evidence: "Each question shows its choices and a proposed answer that names its source, and the product owner confirms or corrects each one." / Rules & behavior covers unconfirmed proposals, no-source proposals and an unreachable memory tier, but never says what happens on a correction or on a reply that skips questions.
    fix:      Add two Rules & behavior lines (and a matching Given/When/Then for each): (1) what happens when the product owner's correction names something that is not among the choices (for example a domain Phoenix memory holds no shelf for) - whether initialize refuses it with a plain message and asks again, or records it with a note that no memory can be set up for it; (2) what happens when the reply leaves some questions unanswered - whether initialize asks again only for those, or stops, and that no unanswered question is recorded as an answer.
